--TEST--
A `spawn script` isolate reads no listener of its parent's, `rule:testing/in-process-request`'s address being the isolate's own — `rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`: `spawn script` goes through a door that asks for
# `script.spawn` first, and deny-by-default means a case with no
# configuration cannot spawn at all. This grants it and nothing else.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE child.nvs--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing`'s isolate shares compiled code and nothing else, and § 18's address
// is context rather than code — so a child never inherits one however its
// parent came by it.
echo "child=", Core\Debug::render(Core\Test::serverUrl()), "\n";
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Both halves, because the child's `null` alone would read the same for a
// runner that had simply never armed anything: the parent is asked the same
// question in the same run, and both answer `null` because neither is a
// `#[Test(server: true)]`.
var $job = spawn script "child.nvs" with(output: "capture");
var $result = await $job;
echo $result->output;
echo "parent=", Core\Debug::render(Core\Test::serverUrl()), "\n";
--EXPECT--
child=null
parent=null
